<h1>Replay recorded traffic</h1>

<p>Real use is the best test suite there is. With <code>$padRecord = TRUE</code> in
<code>_config/config.php</code>, every GET request the application answers with a 200 is kept
with its answer; <code>develop/?replay</code> later asks every one of those pages again, against
the code as it stands, and names each page whose answer changed and the first line where it
parts from the recording.</p>

<ul>
  <li>A name instead of TRUE picks the store, <code>DATA/replay/&lt;name&gt;/</code>, one file per
      URL; <code>?page&amp;padRecord=name</code> records one request of this machine's own.</li>
  <li>Only a request that brought no cookie but PAD's own two ids is recorded: one with a
      session or a login cannot be replayed faithfully, because a replay comes without cookies.</li>
  <li>The host an answer was recorded under counts as the host it is replayed on.</li>
  <li>An answer that changed on purpose is accepted - it becomes the recording - and a page
      that changes every time, a clock, is deleted from the store.</li>
</ul>

<p>A replay must never write. While one runs, <code>db()</code> refuses every statement that
would change the database - it answers 0, as if no row changed - and <code>padFilePut</code>
refuses what the application's own code asks to write:</p>

{example 'fragments/replay_1'}
